    'reasoning_tokens': 625,
    ...
}

Your request reports:

661 completion tokens in total

625 reasoning tokens

36 other completion tokens, approximately

The model used a substantial part of its reported output-token budget on reasoning rather than the final answer you saw.

This helps explain why the response can feel slow even when the visible answer is short.

Important: reasoning tokens are not necessarily displayed as text. The API reports them separately as part of completion usage.

Your input grew from 1,853 to 1,884 tokens between these requests. That's only 31 additional tokens.

Why? Because you already had a fairly large conversation saved in memory.json before starting this session. The new messages added relatively little compared with the existing history.

The bigger issue is that every request continues to carry that existing history.

And there is a second issue: the model may generate hundreds of reasoning tokens to answer a simple question.

These are two separate optimization opportunities:

Problem Potential solution
Too much history sent to the model | Limit the active conversation context
Too many output/reasoning tokens  | Use a model/configuration suited to the task


